  "query_preview": "/MONDAY NIGHT THROUGH SATURDAY/...\nIssued at 1200 AM MDT Sun Oct 4 2026\n\nTemps will warm up once again Monday as relatively light NW flow at \nmid levels induces a lee surface trough. Temps will warm up to \naround 80 on the plains and 70s in the valleys.\n\nFor Tuesday, a bit more moisture will push into the state, \nespecially over the mtns, and we may see scattered pops over the \nhigher terrain, and cannot rule out a shower pushing onto the I-25 \ncorridor (especially in N El Paso county). Temps will warm up a few \ndegrees on this day over the plains, with lower to mid 80s plains \nand 70s valleys.\n\nFrom Wed thru Sat, temps will cool slightly and cannot rule out \nafternoon showers in the mtns, but plains will be dry. Temps will be \naround 80 plains and near 70 valleys.\n\nStatistical guidance (prior to ingesting 00 UTC guidance) begins to \nshow increasing range in temp values starting Sunday as longer range \nguidance is not in agreement. GFS deterministic guidance (prior to \n00 UTC) is leaning towards a more progressive trough early next week \nwhile EC guidance shows a much more amplified pattern. Likewise, GFS \nis much warmer while EC is cooler and potentially more active with \nprecip. With that said, the 00 UTC GFS guidance has a bit more \namplified pattern, similar to the earlier 12 UTC EC guidance. \nIn a nutshell...it appears that the wx may be a bit more active \nat the beginning of the following next week. \\/Hodanish.",
